# Byte-level rules. Order matters: the last matching pattern wins.
#
# 1. Documentation and source are plain text.
*.md text
*.cff text
*.yml text
*.yaml text
*.txt text
*.py text
*.svg text

# 2. Archives and binary artifacts.
*.xz binary
*.7z binary
*.pkl binary
*.npy binary
*.sqlite3 binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
*.docx binary
*.xlsx binary
*.zip binary

# 3. Verbatim bytes. The data files are stored with CRLF line endings and the
#    pipeline's cache manifests compare exact bytes, so git must not normalise them.
#    Generated result tables under experiments/ are also compared byte for byte.
data/** -text
*_raw_features.csv -text
*_raw_features.csv.meta.json -text
experiments/** -text
